Here is the Terraform HCL program that creates a Lambda function URL resource for an `aws_lambda_function` named `example_lambda`. The configuration assumes that the `example_lambda` function is already defined in the same Terraform configuration.

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lambda_function_url" "example_lambda_url" {
  authorization_type = "NONE"
  function_name      = aws_lambda_function.example_lambda.function_name

  cors {
    allow_credentials = false
    allow_headers     = ["Content-Type"]
    allow_methods     = ["GET", "POST"]
    allow_origins     = ["*"]
    expose_headers    = ["Content-Type"]
    max_age           = 300
  }

  timeouts {
    create = "5m"
  }
}
```

This configuration defines a Lambda function URL with the following properties:
- Authorization type set to `NONE` (publicly accessible).
- CORS settings to allow common headers and methods.
- A timeout of 5 minutes for the creation of the URL.

Ensure that the `aws_lambda_function.example_lambda` resource is defined in your Terraform configuration for this to work.

