LLM Output #0:
I will create a Terraform configuration to deploy a serverless Amazon MSK (Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka) cluster with 3 broker nodes. Since MSK is serverless, the number of broker nodes is managed automatically by AWS, but we will specify the desired number of nodes as part of the configuration.

Here is the Terraform HCL program:

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_msk_cluster" "msk_cluster" {
  cluster_name           = "serverless-msk-cluster"
  kafka_version          = "3.3"
  number_of_broker_nodes = 3

  broker_node_group_info {
    client_subnets       = ["us-west-2a", "us-west-2b", "us-west-2c"]
    instance_type        = "kafka.m5.large"
    security_groups      = ["sg-12345678"]
    az_distribution      = "balanced"
  }

  encryption_info {
    encryption_in_transit {
      client_broker = "TLS"
      in_cluster    = true
    }
  }

  logging_info {
    broker_logs {
      cloudwatch_logs_enabled = true
      firehose_enabled        = false
      s3_enabled              = false
    }
  }

  tags = {
    Environment = "dev"
    Project     = "msk-demo"
  }
}
```

This configuration creates a serverless MSK cluster with 3 broker nodes in the `us-west-2` region, using Kafka version 3.3. It specifies the broker node group information, including the client subnets, instance type, and security group. It also enables encryption in transit and logging to CloudWatch. The cluster is tagged with `Environment` and `Project` for better resource management.

