I will generate a Terraform HCL program that creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) using the `aws_lb` resource. The configuration will include a minimal but valid setup with a default VPC, subnet mapping, and basic attributes to ensure the ALB is deployable and functional in a real AWS environment.

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "app_load_balancer" {
  name               = "app-load-balancer"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  ip_address_type    = "ipv4"
  idle_timeout       = 60
  enable_http2       = true

  subnet_mapping {
    subnet_id = "subnet-12345678"
  }

  tags = {
    Environment = "dev"
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration creates an Application Load Balancer in the `us-west-2` region with a default name, HTTP/2 enabled, and a single subnet mapping. The `subnet-12345678` is a placeholder for a valid subnet ID in your AWS environment. You can replace it with an actual subnet ID or create a VPC and subnets using additional Terraform resources if needed.

